      "content": "Ibuprofen can help with pain relief, but it may not directly address the nerve compression or inflammation causing the facial symptoms. Sumatriptan is a more effective option, specifically designed for migraine relief, but it's usually better taken as soon as symptoms start. If you're considering using leftover medication, make sure to follow the label instructions and talk to your doctor about potential interactions with any other medications you're taking. Additionally, over-the-counter triptans like sumatriptan can also be quite potent, so use caution.",
